<title>GERMANY: BMW says 96 DVFA profit 959 mln marks.</title>
<headline>BMW says 96 DVFA profit 959 mln marks.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    DVFA profit				  959     vs 795</p>
<p>    BMW automobiles profit from ord act  2,389   vs 2,185</p>
<p>    Rover group ord act pre-tax loss     279     vs 335</p>
<p>    Aero engines ord act pre-tax loss    627     vs 652</p>
<p>    Financial services profit on ord act  26     vs 102(loss)</p>
<p>NOTE - BMW has already reported the following:</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   820     vs 692</p>
<p>    Group profit from ord activities     1,660   vs 1,367</p>
<p>    Dividend (marks)			   15	vs 13.50</p>
<p>    Dividend on preferred shares (marks) 16	vs 14.50</p>
<p>    Parent net profit			  554.4   vs 534.6</p>
<p>    Group sales				  52,270  vs 46,144</p>
<p>    Car production (units)		 1,143,558 vs 1,098,582</p>
<p>    --of which BMW (units)		   639,433 vs 595,056</p>
<p>    --of which Rover Group (units)	 504,125 vs 503,526</p>
<p>    Motorcycle production (units)	  48,950  vs 52,653</p>
<p>    Workforce (headcount)		    116,112 vs 115,763</p>
<p>    Investment				   3,900   vs 3,477</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German carmaker is Bayerische Motoren Werke AG. Rover results were figured according to German accounting standards only.</p>
<p>--Scott Miller, Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
</text>
